# G9POS — API Rules

Authoritative wire contract: `docs/API-SPEC.md`. These rules summarize it; they must not contradict it.

## Shop-data write endpoint
```
POST /v1/sync/events
```
The POS never creates products, sales, voids, expenses, suppliers, or orders via REST.

Do not create:
- `POST /v1/products`
- `POST /v1/sales`
- `POST /v1/sales/{id}/void`
- `POST /v1/expenses`
- `POST /v1/suppliers`
- `POST /v1/orders`
- `PUT` or `PATCH` on any shop-data resource

## Closed REST writes (not POS CRUD)
```
POST /v1/auth/login | refresh | logout
PATCH /v1/devices/{id}          — rename only
POST /v1/setup                  — first owner, empty-users, deploy-time
POST /v1/users                  — create staff (owner JWT or dashboard_viewer)
POST /v1/devices/{id}/revoke    — owner JWT or dashboard_viewer
POST /v1/catalog/import         — CSV; applies PRODUCT_CREATED / CATEGORY_CREATED / INVENTORY_ADJUSTED
```

## Unauthenticated endpoints (only two)
```
POST /v1/auth/login
POST /v1/setup         — first-owner bootstrap, empty-users only, atomic, no JWT issued
```
All other endpoints require a valid JWT.

## Setup
- Only callable when `users` has zero rows (including soft-deleted)
- Empty-table check and insert are one transaction
- Completed before API is exposed to the public internet
- Rate limited: 5 req/min/IP
- `409 SETUP_ALREADY_COMPLETE` if users already exist
- Then the owner uses `POST /v1/auth/login` as today

## Auth model
```
Owner:            username + password → JWT (role: owner)
Staff:            PIN unlock on device — not a server login factor; no username/password
dashboard_viewer: login_context=dashboard on the same login endpoint
```
PIN hashes are stored on `users.pin` and pulled to devices. PIN is never a server login factor.

`dashboard_viewer` may call only: `POST /v1/users`, `POST /v1/devices/{id}/revoke`, `POST /v1/catalog/import`. It cannot submit sync events.

## JWT
- Access token: 15 minutes
- Refresh token: 30 days
- Cached in `flutter_secure_storage` on device
- Offline grace: expired access token with valid refresh token → load app, queue refresh
- Device revocation: `POST /v1/devices/{id}/revoke` — sets `devices.revoked_at`

## Standard response format — API-SPEC.md §1.4
```go
type APIResponse struct {
    Data  interface{} `json:"data,omitempty"`
    Error *APIError   `json:"error,omitempty"`
    Meta  Meta        `json:"meta"`
}
type APIError struct {
    Code    string `json:"code"`
    Message string `json:"message"`
    Field   string `json:"field,omitempty"`
}
```
Success: `{ data, meta }`. Error: `{ error, meta }`. No `success` flag. `meta.request_id` on every response. `error` is an object, never a string.

Always use `response.OK()`, `response.BadRequest()`, `response.Unauthorized()`, `response.InternalError()` — never `c.JSON()` a different shape.

## Handler pattern
```go
func (h *Handler) GetProducts(c *gin.Context) {
    products, err := h.service.GetAllProducts(c.Request.Context())
    if err != nil {
        slog.Error("get products failed", "error", err)
        response.InternalError(c, "Could not load products")
        return
    }
    response.OK(c, products)
}
```
Never query the database from a handler. Never put business logic in a handler.

## Sync events
```
POST /v1/sync/events
Body: { device_id, events: [...] }
Response: { accepted: [...], rejected: [...], conflicts: [...], stock_corrections: [...] }
```
Each event group is applied atomically. WebSocket broadcast fires only after transaction commits.

`EXPENSE_CREATED`: owner and staff. `EXPENSE_UPDATED` / `EXPENSE_DELETED`: owner only.

## Catalog import
`POST /v1/catalog/import` — owner JWT or `dashboard_viewer`. Validate entire CSV; one transaction; no partial apply. Server UUIDs. `reference_id` NULL on every generated event. Devices receive rows via `GET /v1/sync/pull`.

## GET endpoints (reads)
```
GET /v1/products
GET /v1/users
GET /v1/sync/pull
GET /v1/reports/daily-summary
GET /v1/reports/range
GET /v1/sales
GET /v1/expenses          — owner, staff, dashboard
GET /v1/devices
```

## WebSocket — API-SPEC.md §11
- Dashboard clients only — never POS app
- Path: `wss://api.g9pos.com/ws?token=<access_token>`
- Pushes: `sale.created`, `sale.voided`, `stock.low`, `stock.negative`, `device.sync_status`, `device.activated`
- If WebSocket drops: dashboard falls back to polling `GET /v1/sync/pull` every 30s
- Receive-only — no client → server writes
- Never load-bearing for POS operation

## Error response rules
- Never expose raw Go errors or stack traces to the client
- Error message is plain language, one sentence
- Internal errors logged with full context server-side

## Shop timezone
```go
if !timezone.IsSameShopDay(sale.ServerReceivedAt, time.Now()) {
    return ErrVoidWindowClosed
}
```
Never: `sale.CreatedAt.Day() != time.Now().Day()`
